<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:38:40 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>🔴 French PM vows 'massive' police operation for new protests on Saturday</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-live-curfews-come-into-effect-around-france-to-combat-looting</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">793f3954-cc8b-11f1-8e8f-2b6c5c6d0fa2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:38:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA[France's sociopolitical & economic crises: 'Large portion of population sympathizes' with protestors]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-france-s-sociopolitical-economic-crises-large-portion-of-population-sympathizes-with-protestors</link><description>
Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Damien Leconte, Political Scientist and Researcher at Paris Panthéon Sorbonne University. France’s escalating unrest has exposed a profound contradiction in the state’s response: disproportionate force against peaceful demonstrators on the one hand, and an apparent inability to contain widespread violence on the other. Political scientist Damien Leconte argues that the government’s failure extends beyond policing to the political interpretation of the crisis itself. As competing narratives threaten to overshadow legitimate grievances over education, public services and the cost of living, he warns that “the repressive response […] is not going to make the social crisis disappear.” With presidential elections approaching, the struggle to restore order is becoming inseparable from a deeper contest over political legitimacy, public liberties and the future direction of French society.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f11ae6d6-cc80-11f1-aaa1-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-130312-130947-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f11ae6d6-cc80-11f1-aaa1-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-130312-130947-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f670fe18-cc80-11f1-a285-b9e456527e5c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:32:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Six years on, France remembers slain teacher Samuel Paty</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261020-six-years-on-france-remembers-slain-teacher-samuel-paty</link><description>
French schoolteacher Samuel Paty was killed on October 16, 2020 after false rumours circulated about racism following one of his lessons in which cartoons from the satirical publication Charlie Hebdo were shown. For the first time since his murder, journalists from France Télévisions were allowed to film inside the school where he taught in Conflans-Sainte-Honorine, near Paris. They met a new generation of young people, who are determined to play their part in the fight against terrorism.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07dd9088-cbd9-11f1-b486-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-ECR-FRZ-SAMUEL-PATY-MARCHAIS-Florent.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07dd9088-cbd9-11f1-b486-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-ECR-FRZ-SAMUEL-PATY-MARCHAIS-Florent.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">435e5476-cbd9-11f1-bd0c-4b8fae061dce</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:28:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Florent MARCHAIS</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ivorian DJ digs forgotten tracks, on the hunt for great classics</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-ivorian-dj-digs-forgotten-tracks-on-the-hunt-for-great-classics</link><description>
Cédric Kouamé travels across Ivory Coast to collect old vinyl records before restoring them. The Ivorian DJ hopes to bring national attention to his passion through an official centre dedicated to the country's historical archives, as FRANCE 24's team on the ground reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e84694e-cc82-11f1-9ed1-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-40128c7c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e84694e-cc82-11f1-9ed1-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-40128c7c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47159f18-cc81-11f1-a7d9-1be4b0761cb5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:09:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Midterms 2026: The farmers calling for more migrant workers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-midterms-2026-the-farmers-calling-for-more-migrant-workers</link><description>
As the US midterms approach, immigration is once again dominating the country’s political discourse and Arizona’s largely agricultural Yuma County, just miles from the Mexican border, is no exception. But here, farmers like John Boelts are calling for more legal migrants, warning that without the labour they provide essential crops may go to waste or never be planted at all. France 24’s Sam Ball and Barbara Gabel sent this report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e2330d6-cbd4-11f1-a9eb-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/main-dans-les-champs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e2330d6-cbd4-11f1-a9eb-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/main-dans-les-champs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a023b876-cc84-11f1-ba8e-65b2a060ce5b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:09:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>‘I don't recognise the country I grew up in anymore’: Some Israelis tempted by exile</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261020-i-don-t-recognise-the-country-i-grew-up-in-anymore-some-israelis-are-tempted-by-exile</link><description>
From our special correspondent in Tel Aviv – Since 2023, Israel has experienced an unprecedented brain drain. With the October 27 legislative elections approaching, many graduates are considering leaving the country if the right-wing and far-right coalition led by Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu remains in power.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94bdba32-c96d-11f1-9e3e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/skyline-Tel-Aviv.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94bdba32-c96d-11f1-9e3e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/skyline-Tel-Aviv.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6993a904-cc6d-11f1-b670-01eaf9681e40</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:07:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/94bdba32-c96d-11f1-9e3e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/skyline-Tel-Aviv.jpg">© David Gormezano, FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>David GORMEZANO</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Exiled critic of Rwandan President Kagame found beheaded in Uganda</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-exiled-critic-of-rwandan-president-kagame-found-beheaded-in-uganda</link><description>
Robert Kabera, a former Rwandan soldier living in Uganda, where he had become a vocal critic of his government back home, was found decapitated near Kampala. Rwandan authorities have been accused of assassinating opponents of President Paul Kagame. FRANCE 24's Aurore Bayoud reports from Kigali, Rwanda.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74318ee8-cc82-11f1-a8e7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5355095f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/74318ee8-cc82-11f1-a8e7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5355095f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12942f5a-cc74-11f1-bba5-fd42895681a0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:34:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso resume dialogue with ECOWAS regional bloc</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-niger-mali-and-burkina-faso-resume-dialogue-with-ecowas-regional-bloc</link><description>
Three junta-ruled Sahel states – Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso – on Saturday resumed dialogue with the ECOWAS regional bloc, which they withdrew from more than 18 months ago. They agreed to work towards a “framework agreement” on cooperation. FRANCE 24’s regional correspondent Harold Girard tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dee99ea-cc7e-11f1-9a40-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7a2f75c4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dee99ea-cc7e-11f1-9a40-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7a2f75c4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bfc4b450-cc75-11f1-94e7-630410e1b9e5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:21:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Kenyan cult leader found guilty of murder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261020-kenyan-cult-leader-found-guilty-of-murder</link><description>
In tonight's programme: Kenyan cult leader Paul Mackenzie is convicted of 191 murders, 190 of which were of children. Also, a former Rwandan soldier and outspoken government critic, Robert Kabera, is found decapitated in Uganda. Plus we meet a young Ivorian music lover who travels around the country looking for old-school sounds that need a little TLC. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f871ee72-cc7e-11f1-bb25-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0ac0abc7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f871ee72-cc7e-11f1-bb25-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-0ac0abc7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6fe7542c-cc04-11f1-94b4-e9ecffe55742</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:15:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA['Very poor communicators: Macron & his govt fail to address 'genuine concerns of the French people']]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/very-poor-communicators-macron-his-govt-fail-to-address-genuine-concerns-of-the-french-people</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome Dr Joseph Downing, Senior Lecturer International Relations and Politics at Aston University. French unrest raises questions about political accountability, police exhaustion and the increasingly confrontational relationship between citizens and the state. Downing argues that  France must reassess how the state exercises authority and responds to both violent unrest and legitimate social movements. And he draws attention to France's centralised policing culture, its revolutionary traditions and the wider threat of Russian information warfare.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66fcfa2c-cc6f-11f1-9306-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261019-151050-152231-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/66fcfa2c-cc6f-11f1-9306-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261019-151050-152231-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6d1e9faa-cc6f-11f1-9928-b742de75c72b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:49:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>France imposes curfews after weekend violence, but is it too much or too little?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261020-france-imposes-curfews-after-weekend-violence-but-is-it-too-much-or-too-little</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, October 20: We look at reactions from the French press after President Emmanuel Macron's government announces a curfew in parts of the country. Is it too much or not enough? We also look at what the foreign press from Britain, Germany and the US are saying about the weekend's violence. Meanwhile, the Italian press react to violent looting and destruction of property in Italy as the government there mulls sending in 500 armed troops. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f16b8980-cc4c-11f1-b509-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-20T05-22-28-363Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f16b8980-cc4c-11f1-b509-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-20T05-22-28-363Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">df67d4dc-cc4c-11f1-990b-85c7fbf07cc2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:47:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Horror and disbelief after lawmaker attacked in rural Australia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-horror-and-disbelief-after-lawmaker-attacked-in-rural-australia</link><description>
A rural Australian town felt a mix of horror and disbelief on Tuesday after a highly respected lawmaker was gravely injured in what looked to be a targeted attack. Former nurse and midwife Helen Haines entered parliament in 2019, earning respect across the political divide for her efforts to stamp out corruption and bolster transparency. The 65-year-old was struck by a two-tonne SUV in Wangaratta on Monday afternoon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0d02b4ba-cc67-11f1-8ab9-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-101953-102144-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0d02b4ba-cc67-11f1-8ab9-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-101953-102144-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1460abc2-cc67-11f1-88b8-57c5145ac3a0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:26:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kenyan cult leader guilty on all charges over 191 starvation deaths</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-kenyan-cult-leader-guilty-on-all-charges-over-191-starvation-deaths</link><description>
A self-proclaimed Kenyan preacher and his associates were on Monday found guilty of murdering 190 children and one adult in an infamous starvation cult. Hundreds of bodies have been discovered since 2023 at the cult base inland from the Kenyan beach resort of Malindi, in what became known as the "Shakahola Forest Massacre".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ed1356c-cc67-11f1-8345-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-102213-102409-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ed1356c-cc67-11f1-8345-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-102213-102409-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83e321f0-cc67-11f1-8958-934260b9226f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:25:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Down to Earth</category><title>Indonesia continues to battle wildfires, with nearly 2 million hectares burned</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261020-indonesia-continues-to-battle-wildfires-with-nearly-2-million-hectares-burned</link><description>
Fires in Indonesia have burned through more than 1.9 million hectares of land, according to new data, as the country battles its worst wildfire season in a decade. The blazes have sent toxic smoke across much of Southeast Asia, forcing schools to close and fuelling a rise in respiratory illnesses. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7692e870-cbcf-11f1-aae0-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/202610191145AS-ASIA-WEATHERINDONESIA-WILDFIRE-VOLUNTEE-O.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7692e870-cbcf-11f1-aae0-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/202610191145AS-ASIA-WEATHERINDONESIA-WILDFIRE-VOLUNTEE-O.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2fbedfe4-cbd4-11f1-b5e6-1b78e86d5641</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:23:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Valérie DEKIMPE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sailing from Britanny to Guadeloupe: Route du Rhum village opens ahead of transatlantic race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-sailing-from-britanny-to-guadeloupe-route-du-rhum-village-opens-ahead-of-transatlantic-race</link><description>
Tuesday marked the opening of the race village in Saint-Malo for the Route du Rhum, with the first boats arriving and more expected in the coming days. A fleet of 115 boats is set to depart on November 1 for Guadeloupe in the Caribbean, as competitors prepare to take on this legendary solo sailing race across the Atlantic.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0af0a90-cc67-11f1-abf2-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-102433-102609-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0af0a90-cc67-11f1-abf2-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-102433-102609-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c5e23384-cc67-11f1-9cb0-17b9fc4aebe8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:23:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zelensky accuses US of again failing to warn Kyiv of impending attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-zelensky-accused-partner-countries-of-not-warning-kyiv-of-oncoming-attacks</link><description>
Russia launched fresh attacks on Ukraine’s energy and civilian infrastructure this Monday. The Ukrainian president said Kyiv had once again received no advance warning of the attacks from partner countries that had previously shared intelligence. He also accused the US of deliberately delaying EU-paid weapons delivery. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d22e1af6-cc6f-11f1-8372-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e7a5d401.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d22e1af6-cc6f-11f1-8372-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e7a5d401.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29336b4c-cc68-11f1-9bbd-910471340474</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:16:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France first night under targeted curfews passes calmly</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-france-first-night-under-targeted-curfews-passed-calmly</link><description>
France’s first night under curfew passed without incident, as authorities sought to restore order following a weekend of demonstrations that escalated into riots. The government will impose further curfews where necessary on Tuesday, Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said. FRANCE 24 International Affairs Editor Philip Turle tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3f122b2-cc69-11f1-aef1-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c016885d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3f122b2-cc69-11f1-aef1-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c016885d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9f764c94-cc67-11f1-8aa0-6b91629f757e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:01:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>French retailers begin filing insurance claims after weekend of looting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261020-french-retailers-begin-filing-insurance-claims-after-weekend-of-looting</link><description>
Shop owners in France are counting the cost of the weekend's riots as the government works on new measures to help them recover from widespread looting. Also in this edition: Germany welcomes new investments from Nvidia into its tech scene, and energy prices continue to climb after new Houthi attacks in Saudi Arabia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b4820d6-cc60-11f1-91a3-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/BUSINESS-DAILY-201026.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b4820d6-cc60-11f1-91a3-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/BUSINESS-DAILY-201026.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b63bcfd4-cc5e-11f1-938a-01abeb67e148</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:57:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Bryan QUINN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France protests: Govt to impose new curfews where 'situation requires it'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-france-protests-govt-to-impose-new-curfews-where-situation-requires-it</link><description>
Following weekend protests and riots across the country, curfews have been imposed by the government in some parts of Paris and several cities in France. In Paris, the night passed without any disturbance as FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports. French Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said that local authorities can decide to extend curfews if necessary.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/93c7ead4-cc66-11f1-a102-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T084944Z-1366507805-RC295OAGBILX-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/93c7ead4-cc66-11f1-a102-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T084944Z-1366507805-RC295OAGBILX-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a55443e-cc66-11f1-930a-a97114b53fe2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:49:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Macron secures diesel deals on Gulf visit as fuel prices stoke unrest in France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261020-macron-secures-diesel-deals-on-gulf-visit-as-fuel-prices-stoke-unrest-in-france</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron has obtained commitments to deliver an additional 200,000 tonnes of diesel per month from the United Arab Emirates and Bahrain during a tour of the Gulf, his office said Tuesday as the French government scrambles to address a cost-of-living crisis that has fuelled unrest in the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdd10518-cc67-11f1-a27b-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292640855386.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdd10518-cc67-11f1-a27b-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292640855386.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83a39c82-cc68-11f1-ad2c-0f7ccea76ac8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:44:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdd10518-cc67-11f1-a27b-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26292640855386.jpg">© WAM via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>The Louvre Museum blocked as France grapples with growing protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-louvre-museum-targeted-as-student-protests-intensify-after-the-weekend</link><description>
Dozens of students gathered outside the Louvre Museum on Monday in an attempt to block access to the iconic landmark. The movement puts pressure on the government as the Yellow Vest movement also grows. Following Saturday’s demonstrations, calls on social media for further protests on October 24 and 31 are multiplying.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40311cdc-cc67-11f1-89b4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e939e1bb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40311cdc-cc67-11f1-89b4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e939e1bb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fba3c0c8-cc62-11f1-ace2-875dfa20485a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:40:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Out of control? France stunned by October 17 rioting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261020-out-of-control-france-stunned-by-october-17-rioting</link><description>
France didn't just erupt on Saturday – it exploded. Police were doubly overwhelmed by the turnout of the October 17 cost-of-living demonstrations, which saw two and-a-half times the crowds they expected. Officers were also overwhelmed by determined flashmobs: some radical militants hellbent on a fight, others who came for the looting. The whole world watched the assault on symbols of the Republic like the 19th-century city hall in Limoges, the usually quiet porcelain capital of France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c8458e-cc64-11f1-9322-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-363d0676.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c8458e-cc64-11f1-9322-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-363d0676.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd0ced18-cbe5-11f1-b77e-e79d49fa3b4f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:08:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Amnesty on Turkish media crackdown: 'Disinformation flourishes when media landscape's narrowed down'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/amnesty-on-turkish-media-crackdown-disinformation-flourishes-when-media-landscape-s-narrowed-down</link><description>
The state takeover of Halk TV, one of Turkey’s most widely watched news channels, represents far more than an isolated confrontation between the authorities and an independent broadcaster. For Milena Buyum, Amnesty International’s Turkey campaigner, it is part of a broader erosion of media pluralism, characterized by the appointment of state trustees, the detention of journalists and mounting restrictions on independent digital platforms. Buyum describes the intervention as a "brutal attack on media freedom in Turkey,” framing it within a sustained crackdown on independent journalism that has intensified since March 2025. 
